         <notesStmt>
            <note type="project" target="#dat1">These notes were likely made in 1887 or early 1888.</note>     
            
            <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.00315" cert="high">This leaf has trial titles on both sides. Whitman published a poem titled "A Carol Closing Sixty-Nine" in the May 21, 1888, issue of the <hi rend="italic">New York Herald</hi>. The poem was then included in <hi rend="italic">November Boughs</hi> later that year. The titles on this sheet, however, appear to be for a cluster, section, or even a separate volume. Similar notes on another manuscript (see <ref target="loc.00016">duk.00056</ref>) suggest that these were early ideas for the "Sands at Seventy" cluster of poems in <hi rend="italic">November Boughs</hi>, in which the poem "A Carol Closing Sixty-Nine" appeared.</note>
         </notesStmt>
